\section{Parameters: units, ranges and defaults}{
\describe{
\item{\code{path}}{path; required. Any of the file types readers formats lists (36 at mzLib 1.0.592), including spectra files and the Bruker .d directories.}
\item{\code{offset}}{int; in \strong{records}; default \code{0}; range \code{>= 0}. Skip this many records. A window, not a cursor: mzLib parses the whole file on every call, so paging re-reads it. For a large file use out in one call.}
\item{\code{limit}}{int; in \strong{records}; default absent; range \code{>= 0}. Return at most this many records. Absent means no limit; there is deliberately no default cap.}
\item{\code{out}}{path; default absent. Write the selected window as a tab-separated table here instead of returning columns (header = column_names). Must differ from path. Parent directories are created.}
}
}
\section{Returned fields}{
Each field with its type, its unit, and what \code{NA} means when it is \code{NA}.

\describe{
\item{\code{path}}{string; never \code{NA}. Absolute path of the input.}
\item{\code{file_type}}{string; never \code{NA}. The SupportedFileType mzLib dispatched, not a guess from the extension.}
\item{\code{reader}}{string; never \code{NA}. The mzLib reader class that parsed it.}
\item{\code{record_type}}{string; never \code{NA}. The mzLib record class the columns are properties of (e.g. ToppicPrsm, MzIdentMLRecord, ProteinGroupFromTsv), so a column is cross-referenceable against the mzLib source.}
\item{\code{views}}{string[]; never \code{NA}. The cross-format views this file also offers; same values as readers formats.}
\item{\code{record_count}}{int; in \strong{records}; never \code{NA}. Records mzLib parsed from the whole file, before the window. Records, not lines: see caveats.}
\item{\code{returned_count}}{int; in \strong{records}; never \code{NA}. Records in columns; 0 when written to out.}
\item{\code{offset}}{int; in \strong{records}; never \code{NA}. The offset applied.}
\item{\code{truncated}}{bool; never \code{NA}. True whenever records were left out by offset or limit.}
\item{\code{excluded_fields}}{table; never \code{NA}. Every property of record_type that could not become a column, as \{field, type, reason, verb\}: nested objects, lists of composites, and dictionaries (reason starts "a dictionary"). verb names the command that carries the field (sample_groups: readers read-protein-groups; samples: readers read-quantified-peptides; mzIdentML scores: readers read-matches) or is null. Empty when every property projects.}
\item{\code{error}}{object; \code{NA} when always, for a single path: a file that cannot be read fails the call instead. \{kind, type, message\}; non-null only in a files[] entry under on-error skip.}
\item{\code{failed_fields}}{string[]; never \code{NA}. "field: ExceptionType" for every property that threw while being read on a returned record; those cells are null.}
\item{\code{column_names}}{string[]; never \code{NA}. The record type's projectable public properties in snake_case, base class first, in declaration order.}
\item{\code{records} (wire \code{columns})}{table; \code{NA} when the table was written to out instead. Column name to per-record values, in column_names order.}
\item{\code{output}}{object; \code{NA} when out was not given. \{path, format: "tsv", row_count\} when out was given; row_count is the window written, not the whole file.}
}
}
\section{Columns of \code{records}}{
The columns are \strong{per format}: this file's own mzLib record fields, named in \code{column_names}. Every cell follows these rules:

\itemize{
\item A cell is null when mzLib's value is null, when a double is NaN or infinite (JSON cannot carry it), or when the property threw (then named in failed_fields).
\item -1 crosses unchanged: in a format's own columns it is often a real measurement. The one exception is retention_time and monoisotopic_mass on IQuantifiableRecord types (psmtsv, osmtsv, MsFraggerPsm, DiaNnReport), where mzLib documents -1 as absent; those are null, matching read-results.
\item Units are the writing tool's and are not normalised: retention time is minutes for psmtsv/osmtsv/MsFraggerPsm/DiaNnReport and undeclared for the rest. read-records carries no retention_time_unit; use a typed view when units matter.
\item Enums cross as their member names, dates as ISO 8601 strings, and a list of scalars as ONE ';'-joined string, on the wire and in out alike; split it yourself.
\item A column named in absent_fields is null in every row, whatever default mzLib filled in.
}
}
